# Maintenance Desk prepares a shift plan from inbox.txt in the current folder.
Use the intake chapter.

A trade is one of plumbing, lighting or joinery.
For a trade, plumbing means "taps, drains, sinks and supply fittings".
For a trade, lighting means "lamps, light fittings and switches".
For a trade, joinery means "doors, shelves, drawers and woodwork".

A priority is one of routine, prompt or urgent.
For a priority, routine means "cosmetic, or fully usable until a later shift".
For a priority, prompt means "inconvenient but a workaround exists".
For a priority, urgent means "the room or essential fixture cannot be used".

A ticket has a location (text), a quote (money), a description (text), a craft (trade, if any), a rank (priority, if any), a handoff (text) and a reason (text).
A ticket can be eligible.
A ticket can be scheduled.
A ticket's quote is never less than $0.

Let the opening budget always be $300.
Let the remaining budget be the opening budget.
Let the intake count be 0.
Let the rejected count be 0.
Let the intake notes be "".

To accept a record (text):
  Add 1 to the intake count.
  Let the cells be the columns of the record.
  If the number of items in the cells is not 3:
    Fail because "expected location|estimated dollars|description".
  Let the site be (item 1 of the cells) or else "".
  Let the price be (item 2 of the cells) or else "".
  Let the note be (item 3 of the cells) or else "".
  Let the dollars be the price as a number.
  If the dollars is nothing:
    Fail because "the estimate must be a number".
  If the dollars is less than 0:
    Fail because "the estimate must be zero or greater".
  Let the cents be the dollars * 100.
  If the cents is not (the cents rounded to the nearest 1):
    Fail because "the estimate must be an amount in whole cents".
  If (the number of items in the words of the site is 0) or (the number of items in the words of the note is 0):
    Fail because "the location and description are required".
  There is a new ticket called "M-{the intake count}" whose location is the site and whose quote is $1 * the dollars and whose description is the note and whose handoff is the note and whose reason is "Awaiting assessment".

To work out the brief (text) of a report (text), ask the model "Write one factual sentence for the next maintenance shift. Summarize the reported problem without promising a repair.".

To assess a ticket:
  If the ticket's quote is more than $200:
    Set the ticket's reason to "Supervisor approval required for estimates over $200".
    Stop.
  Try:
    Judge "Which trade owns this repair?" about the ticket's description and let the pick (trade) be the verdict and the certainty (percent) be the likelihood.
    Judge "How urgently does the reported loss of use need attention?" about the ticket's description and let the level (priority) be the grade.
    Set the ticket's rank to the level.
    If the certainty is less than 50%:
      Set the ticket's reason to "Trade uncertain; supervisor review".
      Stop.
    If the certainty is less than 85%:
      Try:
        Ask the model "Which single maintenance trade should own this repair? Use the description independently." about the ticket's description and let the second opinion (trade) be the reply.
        If the second opinion is not the pick:
          Set the ticket's reason to "Trade opinions disagree; supervisor review".
          Stop.
      If that fails:
        Set the ticket's reason to "Second opinion unavailable; supervisor review ({the problem})".
        Stop.
    Set the ticket's craft to the pick.
    Now the ticket is eligible.
  If that fails:
    Set the ticket's reason to "Assessment unavailable; supervisor review".
    Stop.
  Try:
    Set the ticket's handoff to the brief of the ticket's description.
  If that fails:
    Set the ticket's handoff to "{the ticket's description} [Original report. Handoff unavailable: {the problem}]".

To allocate a band (priority):
  For each eligible ticket:
    If the ticket's rank is nothing:
      Skip this ticket.
    If the ticket's rank is not the band:
      Skip this ticket.
    Let the selected trade be the ticket's craft.
    If the selected trade is nothing:
      Skip this ticket.
    If the ticket's quote is more than the remaining budget:
      Set the ticket's reason to "Wait for next shift budget".
      Skip this ticket.
    Let the occupied be 0.
    For each earlier in scheduled tickets:
      If the earlier has a craft:
        If the earlier's craft is the selected trade:
          Add 1 to the occupied.
    If the occupied is at least 2:
      Set the ticket's reason to "Wait for next crew slot".
      Skip this ticket.
    Now the ticket is scheduled.
    Subtract the ticket's quote from the remaining budget.
    Set the ticket's reason to "Scheduled".

Let the entries be the lines of the file "inbox.txt".
For each entry in the entries:
  If the entry is "":
    Skip this entry.
  Try:
    Accept the entry.
  If that fails:
    Add 1 to the intake count.
    Add 1 to the rejected count.
    Set the intake notes to "{the intake notes}Rejected M-{the intake count}: {the problem}{new line}".

For each ticket:
  Assess the ticket.
Allocate urgent.
Allocate prompt.
Allocate routine.

Let the plan be "MAINTENANCE DESK | SHIFT PLAN{new line}{the intake notes}".
For each ticket:
  Let the crew be "unassigned".
  If the ticket has a craft:
    Set the crew to "{the ticket's craft}".
  Let the urgency be "ungraded".
  If the ticket has a rank:
    Set the urgency to "{the ticket's rank}".
  Set the plan to "{the plan}{the ticket} | {the ticket's location} | {the ticket's quote} | {the crew} | {the urgency} | {the ticket's reason}{new line}  {the ticket's handoff}{new line}".
Let the reserved be the opening budget - the remaining budget.
Set the plan to "{the plan}Scheduled {the number of scheduled tickets} of {the number of tickets}. Reserved {the reserved}. Remaining {the remaining budget}. Rejected {the rejected count}.".
For example, the remaining budget is at least $0.
For example, the reserved + the remaining budget is the opening budget.
For example, the number of tickets + the rejected count is the intake count.
Write the plan to the file "shift-plan.txt".
Say the plan.
